        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371-a1-a7">

                <pb facs="0544" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg470"/>


                <head>Mr. Markham to Mr. G. F.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 381.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Her Majesty’s Consulate</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Shanghai</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 3, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter of yesterday’s
                    date, I have the honor to inform you that considerable trouble was taken in
                    July, 1863, to get at the truth of rumors then current that Burgevine was
                    organizing an expedition to Soochow, and that numerous arrests were made of
                    persons supposed to be implicated.</p>
                <p>Your other question is rather difficult to answer, as the evidence, both with
                    regard to the Firefly and Feeloong, was far from complete. From what I remember
                    of the case I am induced personally to exonerate Burgevine from any direct share
                    in the Firefly piracy.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient, humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. MARKHAM, <hi rendition="#italic">Her Majesty’s Vice
                        Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. F. Seward</hi>, Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
